%T A397966 1420442,1978080,2686442,3570000,4656122,5973120,7552202,9425520,
%U A397966 11628122,14196000,17168042,20584080,24486842,28920000,33930122,39564720,45874202,52909920,60726122
%N A397966 Number of points with even coordinate sum in the 5-dimensional hypercube [-n,n]^5 having an odd number of lattice neighbors inside the hypercube.
%C A397966 Points with an odd number of interior neighbors are exactly those with an odd number of coordinates equal to +-n. A corner's coordinate sum has parity n*d, so in odd dimensions the 32 corners enter the count exactly when n is even, producing a parity defect of (3^d+1)/2 = 122. The corresponding defect is 14 for d = 3 (A398862) and 0 in every even dimension. Proof of the formula: the points with exactly k coordinates equal to +-n number binomial(d,k)*2^k*(2*n-1)^(d-k). Summing over odd k only, via ((2*n-1)+2)^d - ((2*n-1)-2)^d = (2*n+1)^d - (2*n-3)^d, gives twice the count of points with an odd number of extremal coordinates. Imposing even coordinate sum halves this again up to a correction, since among the 2*n-1 free values the counts of even and odd differ by one, in a direction depending on the parity of n. That correction is the constant C, which is independent of n.
%H A397966 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A397966/b397966.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A397966 <a href="/index/Rec#order_06">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (4,-5,0,5,-4,1).
%F A397966 a(n) = 80*n^4 - 160*n^3 + 280*n^2 - 200*n + 61 + 61*(-1)^n.
%F A397966 G.f.: 2*x^2*(421 + 356*x + 966*x^2 + 116*x^3 + 61*x^4)/((1 - x)^5*(1 + x)).
%F A397966 E.g.f.: 2*((61 + 180*x^2 + 160*x^3 + 40*x^4)*cosh(x) + 20*x^2*(9 + 8*x + 2*x^2)*sinh(x) - 61). - _Stefano Spezia_, Aug 20 2026
%e A397966 For n = 2 the hypercube [-2,2]^5 has 3125 points, of which a(2) = 842 have even coordinate sum and an odd number of the 10 lattice neighbors still inside.
%t A397966 A397966[n_] := 61*((-1)^n + 1) + 40*(n-1)*n*(2*(n-1)*n + 5);
%t A397966 Array[A397966, 35] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Aug 26 2026 *)
%o A397966 (PARI) a(n) = 80*n^4 - 160*n^3 + 280*n^2 - 200*n + 61 + 61*(-1)^n
%o A397966 (Python) def a(n): return 80*n**4 - 160*n**3 + 280*n**2 - 200*n + 61 + 61*(-1)**n
